## 3. `next-image-export-optimizer` usage

Illu itself does **not** import `next-image-export-optimizer` directly — it delegates to `ImageZoom`. The actual usage is in `/home/agent/workspace/src/components/image-zoom.tsx`:

```tsx
import ExportedImage, {
	type ExportedImageProps,
} from 'next-image-export-optimizer'
...
export type ImageZoomProps = ExportedImageProps & {
	zoomInProps?: ImgHTMLAttributes<HTMLImageElement>
	rmiz?: UncontrolledProps
	alt?: string
}

export function ImageZoom({ zoomInProps, children, rmiz, alt = '', ...props }: ImageZoomProps) {
	return (
		<Zoom zoomMargin={20} wrapElement="span" {...rmiz} zoomImg={zoomInProps}>
			{children ?? (
				<ExportedImage
					sizes="(max-width: 768px) 100vw, (max-width: 1200px) 70vw, 900px"
					alt={alt}
					{...props}
				/>
			)}
		</Zoom>
	)
}
```

`Illu` passes `src`, `width={640}`, `height={480}`, `alt` as `...props`, which land on `<ExportedImage>` via spread (since Illu passes no `children` to `ImageZoom`). Config in `/home/agent/workspace/next.config.mjs` (lines 6–22):

```js
images: {
	loader: 'custom',
	imageSizes: [640, 960, 1280, 1600, 1920],
	deviceSizes: [640, 960, 1280, 1600, 1920],
},
transpilePackages: ['next-image-export-optimizer'],
env: {
	nextImageExportOptimizer_imageFolderPath: 'public',
	nextImageExportOptimizer_exportFolderPath: 'out',
	nextImageExportOptimizer_quality: '75',
	nextImageExportOptimizer_storePicturesInWEBP: 'true',
	nextImageExportOptimizer_exportFolderName: '_optimized',
	nextImageExportOptimizer_generateAndUseBlurImages: 'true',
},
```
The `build` script (`package.json`) runs `next build && next-image-export-optimizer` to generate the `_optimized` WEBP variants at build time.

